==Political parties==
A total of 24 [[List of political parties in the Dominican Republic|political parties]] were represented on the electoral ballot, including the two large parties and 22 small parties. The small parties are those which do not receive more than 10% of the vote and which are clearly not directly rivaling the main candidates. These parties generally choose to ally themselves with one of the large parties.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.jce.gob.do/portals/0/Elecciones2012/boletines/B12_PconAlianzas.html|title=Resultados Elecciones Presidenciales y Vicepresidenciales y de Diputados (as) de Ultramar|accessdate=19 June 2012|date=29 May 2012}}</ref> Thirteen parties were previously rejected by the Central Electoral Commission.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.listin.com.do/la-republica/2012/1/22/218970/Critican-que-la-Junta-Central-Electoral-haya-rechazado-partidos|title=Critican que JCE haya rechazado a partidos|accessdate=22 April 2012|date=22 January 2012}}</ref>
